  "name": "Hepatitis Core Antibody - Hbc Total",
  "code": "HBC total",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<table><thead><tr><th><div>Anti-HBc Total Test Result</div></th><th><div>Interpretation</div></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><div>Positive</div></td><td><div>A positive result for Anti-HBc Total indicates previous exposure to the Hepatitis B virus (HBV). It does not distinguish between acute or resolved infections. The presence of Anti-HBc Total antibodies suggests either a past HBV infection that has been cleared by the immune system (resolved infection) or an ongoing HBV infection (chronic infection). Further testing, including HBsAg and HBV DNA tests, may be needed to determine the current status of the infection and the individual's HBV carrier state.</div></td></tr><tr><td><div>Negative</div></td><td><div>A negative result for Anti-HBc Total indicates no previous exposure to HBV. The individual is susceptible to HBV infection and should consider vaccination, especially if they are at risk of exposure to the virus.</div></td></tr></tbody></table>",
